  "id": "COMPOUND:30029 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "Cassialactone is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SK-VLB through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Cassialactone targets Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a known target of 5-Oxobrucine and Dendridine A. These compounds, in turn, target SK-VLB, indicating a potential cascade of interactions where Cassialactone may influence SK-VLB through its effect on Microtubule-associated protein 1B. The presence of multiple targets (5-Oxobrucine and Dendridine A) further supports the idea that Cassialactone may modulate the activity of these proteins, which in turn affect SK-VLB. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Cassialactone could interact with SK-VLB, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
